# Backrest migration — 2026-10-23

Active scheduling now lives in Backrest at http://127.0.0.1:9898/.
The shell profiles and scripts below remain available for manual use and rollback.
All five legacy Restic LaunchAgents (15m, hourly, daily, watchdog, Seaback)
are persistently disabled and unloaded. The in-flight legacy hourly run was
terminated cleanly during cutover without saving that run; existing snapshots
were preserved. Backrest's first scheduled personal backup is now running.

- `lshq-15m`, `erebusbat-15m`, and `lshq-docs`: every 15 minutes.
- `lshq-hourly` and `erebusbat-hourly`: minute 55 of each hour.
- `lshq-daily` and `erebusbat-daily`: 14:15 local time.
- `seaback-daily` and `seaback-weekly`: check at minute 35 each hour;
  run only when 24 hours / 7 days have elapsed since a successful backup.
  Failed, partial, and dry-run backups do not advance these timestamps.
  A disconnected disk or a not-yet-due tier cancels that attempt and retries
  next hour. This gate also applies to Backrest's manual Backup Now button;
  the existing `seaback/run daily` or `weekly` command can force a manual run.

Seaback's exclusion list is **`~/.restic/seaback-excludes.lst`**.
The legacy Seaback script and both Backrest plans use this same file.
The other existing exclusion lists remain in `~/.restic`.

Backrest config: `~/.config/backrest/config.json` (contains secrets, mode 0600).
Service: `~/Library/LaunchAgents/sh.brew.backrest.plist`.
`BACKREST_RESTIC_COMMAND` selects `~/.restic/backrest-restic`, which:

- Uses the installed `/opt/homebrew/bin/restic` and prevents idle sleep while it runs.
- Validates Seaback's volume UUID, mount point, repository ID, and protected-folder
  readability before a backup; never initializes a repository automatically.
- Advances Seaback's success markers only after a non-dry-run backup exits zero.
- Maps the shared `maze` repository's container SSH-key path to this Mac's
  `~/.ssh/id_rsync_ed25519`, with batch mode and strict host-key checking.

The shared `rsyncnet` repository retains ownership by `maze` and its original
sync permissions; local personal plans reference it. The `lshq` repository uses
its existing password file and SSH alias. All nine migrated plans keep all
snapshots. Existing Seaback maintenance policies are preserved. No new retention
or automatic deletion policy was added.

The inactive `profile-erebusbat-s3.sh` fallback could not be verified during the
migration and remains a manual shell profile; it has no Backrest plan.

Validation: repository access/dry runs through the Backrest service; a Seaback
one-file backup and restore verified byte-for-byte; a real `lshq-docs` plan
backup; Seaback dry-run cadence-state verification; shell and plist validation.
Full daily/weekly data coverage and a complete disaster-recovery restore have
not been tested. A small snapshot tagged `backrest-migration-verification`
remains in Seaback as validation evidence.

Original config, service plists, Seaback script/excludes, and this README were
saved under `/Users/andrew.burns/.restic/backrest-migration-20261023-115229` (private directory). The original disabled-service state is
in `original-disabled.txt`. To roll back, stop Backrest, restore its config and
service plist from that directory, then re-enable/bootstrap only the desired
legacy agents. Do not run both scheduling systems concurrently. The old
Seaback agent was already disabled before this migration.

Homebrew may regenerate its LaunchAgent during service reinstall; preserve the
`BACKREST_RESTIC_COMMAND` environment setting when doing so.

